Verse 1:
[C/E]Christ is [G7]alive! [C]Let [F/C]Christians [C/G]sing.
[C/E]His [G]cross [F/C]stands [C]empty [F]to [C/G]the [G]sky.
[G]Let [F#m]streets [G]and homes [C/G]with [G]praises ring.
[G]His [C/G]love [Dm/A]in [F]death [G]shall [Dm/A]never [G]die.

Verse 2:
[C/E]Christ [G7]is [C]alive!
[C/E]No [F/C]longer [C/G]bound
[G]To [F#m]distant [G]years [C/G]in [G]Palestine,
[G]He [F#m]comes [G]to claim [C/G]the [G]here [F#m]and [G]now
[G]And [C/G]conquer [F]every [C/G]place [G]and [C/E]time.

Verse 3:
[C/E]In every [G7/F]insult,
[C/E]rift, and [F]war
[G]Where [F#m]color, [G]scorn [C/G]or [G]wealth [F#m]divide,
[G]He [F#m]suffers [G]still, yet [C/G]loves [F#m]the [G]more,
